            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 31,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there a follow-on commit which shows the benefit of splitting this out? (Since current callers are not needing this I'm assuming this is in preparation for another commit.)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 31,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "The purpose of this commit is to allow json-output generation based on the content of LogEntry.\n\n\n```\n  std::optional<DbusEventLogEntry> optEntry =\n        fillDbusEventLogEntryFromPropertyMap(propertyMap);\n   if( COND(*optEntry) )\n   {\n      Json-output generation\n   }\n```\n\nAt this time, there is no immediate upstream follow-up commits unlike the case of IBM-downstream which will do the conditional json-output"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 31,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not sure I understand why this is needed.  What does \"conditional json-output\" mean?  Is there a commit you can point me to?\n\nAs written, this is adding code for the same use cases.  That's fine if we have a feature that we need for this, but we need to articulate the feature."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 31,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "I reworded the commit message to show a possible example (Oem-specific need) to check the condition."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/log_services.hpp",
                    "line": 1809,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "nit, *entry works just as well and avoids a whole line"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/log_services.hpp",
                    "line": 1809,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
